# Odd-weight parabolic cohomology comparison at level three

Theorem statement: `MTT.Cohomology.parabolicH1_finrank_le_level_three_odd`
(`03513b57-2878-4a4a-8605-3db4bbbcae31`), by cbirkbeck, 2026-09-08.

Proof: submission `b7503d44-7081-47cf-9b15-657b1a0ca313`, by cbirkbeck, 2026-09-08 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

For every odd integer $k\ge3$, the degree-$k-2$ parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma_1(3)$ satisfies

$$\dim_{\mathbf C}H^1_{\mathrm{par}}(\Gamma_1(3),\operatorname{Sym}^{k-2}\mathbf C^2)\le
2\dim_{\mathbf C}S_k(\Gamma_1(3)).$$

This isolates level three after treating the level-four cohomological estimate by explicit
generators. Its order-three elliptic contribution must be retained; the torsion-free large-level
formula does not apply.

## Explanation of the source proof

# Combining the level-three numeric bounds

For an odd weight (k\ge3), the degree (n=k-2) is positive and odd.
The separately submitted generator-and-elliptic calculation gives

$$\dim H^1_{\mathrm{par}}(\Gamma_1(3),\operatorname{Sym}^{k-2}\mathbf C^2)
\le 2\bigl(\lfloor k/3\rfloor-1\bigr).$$

The remaining cusp-form input is

$$\lfloor k/3\rfloor-1\le\dim S_k(\Gamma_1(3)).$$

Twice this second inequality, followed by transitivity, proves the desired
comparison. This is a formal reduction: it keeps the cusp-form lower bound
as an explicit open dependency, rather than importing Eichler--Shimura
surjectivity or assuming the whole mission. The cohomological estimate is
independent of that analytic lower bound. The submitted reduction contains
no admitted step or resource-limit override.

